_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:17:## Top 3 must-fix
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:18:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:19:1. **Tailwind's `dark:` variant is bound to the OS media query, not the site's `.dark` class.** No `@custom-variant dark` exists anywhere; the built CSS puts all `dark:` utilities inside one `@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark)` block. Same element, site theme dark both times: OS-light → `bg-blue-50` (near-white), OS-dark → `dark:bg-blue-950/30`. 370 `dark:` utilities are affected; six Callouts on this essay render light-grey text on a white panel. One line fixes it.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:20:2. **`--accent` never paints.** `global.css:116/:170` set the real violet, then `:1770/:1792` (leftover shadcn) override it with bare HSL triples at equal specificity. Measured on `.reading-companion__header`: token = `217.2 32.6% 17.5%`, computed colour = `--text-primary`. 19 live elements plus the reading-progress bar, which paints nothing.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:21:3. **`ReadingCompanion` never sticks.** `xl:self-start` (`PostLayout.astro:211`) caps the grid item at content height, so the sticky child has no travel. Measured: rect top 457 → −402 across 859px of scroll (1:1, no pinning), off-screen by `scrollY ≈ 2462` while the article is 23306px tall. Violates V5 and §7 item 3 directly.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:22:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/opus-taste-p0bc.log:23:A4 (Evidence Focus unreachable — 0 evidence links outside `<template>`, verified statically and in the live DOM) is close behind and arguably the worst *functional* gap.
