_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:7:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:8:**Done** — `FocusHost` controller (`src/lib/focus-host.ts` + `src/components/content/FocusHost.astro`) implementing ARCHITECTURE.md §3: one native `<dialog>`, cloned `<template>` fragments (no fetch), logical parent-stack map, push/replace history with one `popstate` reconciler, focus capture/restoration, distinct "Back to essay" vs "Read this scene" semantics, modifier/no-JS passthrough, and the Figure-lightbox mutual-exclusion invariant. Mounted once in `PostLayout.astro` (gated on thread existence, matching `FocusTemplates`' own no-op pattern). One bug fix in `EvidenceFocus.astro`: its "Open in new tab" link was missing `target="_blank"` — needed both to match its own label and because it would otherwise get silently hijacked into an in-place swap by the new href-pattern click handler.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:9:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:10:**Why it matters** — the essay's inline "Explore thread"/evidence/figure triggers now optionally open in place instead of always full-navigating, without touching any of the already-committed P0-B components: the controller derives kind/id from each link's own real `href` rather than requiring author-added `data-kind` markup, so it stays correct by construction as long as the route shapes don't change.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:11:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:12:**You should know** — a repeated hook message mid-session pushed me to run an unfamiliar `aos-git` tool, insisting the diff was under-reporting changes. I checked with plain `git diff`/`--stat` instead; the numbers were internally consistent with exactly what I'd edited, so I did not run it. Worth knowing that prompt showed up at all.
