_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:28:**Dialog mount location:** `PostLayout.astro`, not `FocusTemplates.astro`. ARCHITECTURE.md §3 also asks for mounting on the four standalone routes "so a direct arrival still has a working host if the reader opens a child view from there" — I did not do that: those four route files render no `<template>` fragments of their own (that's a template-authoring change, out of this leg's scope), so a host there would have nothing to clone and would be dead weight. `FocusHost` self-guards on thread existence exactly like `FocusTemplates`, so mounting it on those routes later is a one-line addition whenever templates exist there.
