_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:40:| N07 | **Pass** (by construction) | Fully static pages with no server session state — a refresh is byte-identical to a direct load; verified via the same curl output. |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:41:| N08 | Not runnable | Modifier-click passthrough needs a real browser to dispatch a modified click event; verified in code only (handler returns early on `ctrlKey/metaKey/shiftKey/altKey/button!==0` before any `preventDefault`). |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:42:| N09 | **Pass** (verified via code + curl, not a literal JS-disabled browser) | Every trigger remains a real `<a href>`; without JS no listener attaches at all, so the browser's default navigation goes straight to the already-verified-working standalone routes (N06). No JS-only content exists anywhere in the flow. |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:43:| N10 | Not runnable | Needs simulating `pushState` failure in a live session; verified in code only — `writeHistory` catches, `open()` checks the boolean return and never calls `preventDefault` on failure, so the real `href` fires. |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:44:| N11 | Not runnable | Needs live dialog state to observe the two distinct destinations. |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0c-controller.log:45:| N12 | **Not met as specified** | ARCHITECTURE.md §3 itself only specifies x/y pixel-coordinate restore (not 03_NAVIGATION's fuller anchor+relative-offset algorithm) — I implemented exactly that. It's correct when layout is stable but won't gracefully handle a viewport/content change between open and close. This is a deviation carried from the architecture decision, not something I skipped. |
