_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:48:# Chrome DevTools Agent Skill
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:49:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:50:Browser automation via executable Puppeteer scripts. All scripts output JSON for easy parsing.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:51:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:52:## Quick Start
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:53:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:54:**CRITICAL**: Always check `pwd` before running scripts.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:55:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:56:### Installation
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:57:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:58:#### Step 1: Install System Dependencies (Linux/WSL only)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:59:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:60:On Linux/WSL, Chrome requires system libraries. Install them first:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:61:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:62:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:63:pwd  # Should show current working directory
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:64:cd .claude/skills/chrome-devtools/scripts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:65:./install-deps.sh  # Auto-detects OS and installs required libs
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:66:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:67:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:68:Supports: Ubuntu, Debian, Fedora, RHEL, CentOS, Arch, Manjaro
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:69:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:70:**macOS/Windows**: Skip this step (dependencies bundled with Chrome)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:71:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:72:#### Step 2: Install Node Dependencies
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:73:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:74:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:75:npm install  # Installs puppeteer, debug, yargs
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:76:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:77:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:78:#### Step 3: Install ImageMagick (Optional, Recommended)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:79:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:80:ImageMagick enables automatic screenshot compression to keep files under 5MB:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:81:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:82:**macOS:**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:83:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:84:brew install imagemagick
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:85:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:86:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:87:**Ubuntu/Debian/WSL:**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:88:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:89:sudo apt-get install imagemagick
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:90:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:91:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:92:**Verify:**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:93:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:94:magick -version  # or: convert -version
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:95:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:96:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:97:Without ImageMagick, screenshots >5MB will not be compressed (may fail to load in Gemini/Claude).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:98:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:99:### Test
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:100:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:101:node navigate.js --url https://example.com
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:102:# Output: {"success": true, "url": "https://example.com", "title": "Example Domain"}
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:103:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:104:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:105:## Available Scripts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:106:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:107:All scripts are in `.claude/skills/chrome-devtools/scripts/`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:108:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:109:**CRITICAL**: Always check `pwd` before running scripts.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:110:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:111:### Script Usage
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:112:- `./scripts/README.md`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:113:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:114:### Core Automation
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:115:- `navigate.js` - Navigate to URLs
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:116:- `screenshot.js` - Capture screenshots (full page or element)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:117:- `click.js` - Click elements
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:118:- `fill.js` - Fill form fields
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:119:- `evaluate.js` - Execute JavaScript in page context
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:120:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:121:### Analysis & Monitoring
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:122:- `snapshot.js` - Extract interactive elements with metadata
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:123:- `console.js` - Monitor console messages/errors
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:124:- `network.js` - Track HTTP requests/responses
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:125:- `performance.js` - Measure Core Web Vitals + record traces
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:126:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:127:## Usage Patterns
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:128:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:129:### Single Command
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:130:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:131:pwd  # Should show current working directory
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:132:cd .claude/skills/chrome-devtools/scripts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:133:node screenshot.js --url https://example.com --output ./docs/screenshots/page.png
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:134:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:135:**Important**: Always save screenshots to `./docs/screenshots` directory.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:136:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:137:### Automatic Image Compression
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:138:Screenshots are **automatically compressed** if they exceed 5MB to ensure compatibility with Gemini API and Claude Code (which have 5MB limits). This uses ImageMagick internally:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:139:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:140:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:141:# Default: auto-compress if >5MB
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:142:node screenshot.js --url https://example.com --output page.png
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:143:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:144:# Custom size threshold (e.g., 3MB)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:145:node screenshot.js --url https://example.com --output page.png --max-size 3
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:146:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:147:# Disable compression
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:148:node screenshot.js --url https://example.com --output page.png --no-compress
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:149:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:150:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:151:**Compression behavior:**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:152:- PNG: Resizes to 90% + quality 85 (or 75% + quality 70 if still too large)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:153:- JPEG: Quality 80 + progressive encoding (or quality 60 if still too large)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:154:- Other formats: Converted to JPEG with compression
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:155:- Requires ImageMagick installed (see imagemagick skill)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:156:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:157:**Output includes compression info:**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:158:```json
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:159:{
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:160:  "success": true,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:161:  "output": "/path/to/page.png",
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:162:  "compressed": true,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:163:  "originalSize": 8388608,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:164:  "size": 3145728,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:165:  "compressionRatio": "62.50%",
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:166:  "url": "https://example.com"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:167:}
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:168:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:169:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:170:### Chain Commands (reuse browser)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:171:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:172:# Keep browser open with --close false
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:173:node navigate.js --url https://example.com/login --close false
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:174:node fill.js --selector "#email" --value "user@example.com" --close false
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:175:node fill.js --selector "#password" --value "secret" --close false
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:176:node click.js --selector "button[type=submit]"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:177:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:178:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:179:### Parse JSON Output
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:180:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:181:# Extract specific fields with jq
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:182:node performance.js --url https://example.com | jq '.vitals.LCP'
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:183:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:184:# Save to file
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:185:node network.js --url https://example.com --output /tmp/requests.json
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:186:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:187:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:188:## Execution Protocol
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:189:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:190:### Working Directory Verification
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:191:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:192:BEFORE executing any script:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:193:1. Check current working directory with `pwd`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:194:2. Verify in `.claude/skills/chrome-devtools/scripts/` directory
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:195:3. If wrong directory, `cd` to correct location
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:196:4. Use absolute paths for all output files
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:197:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:198:Example:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:199:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:200:pwd  # Should show: .../chrome-devtools/scripts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:201:# If wrong:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:202:cd .claude/skills/chrome-devtools/scripts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:203:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:204:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:205:### Output Validation
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:206:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:207:AFTER screenshot/capture operations:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:208:1. Verify file created with `ls -lh <output-path>`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:209:2. Read screenshot using Read tool to confirm content
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:210:3. Check JSON output for success:true
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:211:4. Report file size and compression status
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:212:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:213:Example:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:214:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:215:node screenshot.js --url https://example.com --output ./docs/screenshots/page.png
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:216:ls -lh ./docs/screenshots/page.png  # Verify file exists
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:217:# Then use Read tool to visually inspect
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:218:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:219:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:220:5. Restart working directory to the project root.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:221:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:222:### Error Recovery
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:223:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:224:If script fails:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:225:1. Check error message for selector issues
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:226:2. Use snapshot.js to discover correct selectors
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:227:3. Try XPath selector if CSS selector fails
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:228:4. Verify element is visible and interactive
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:229:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:230:Example:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:231:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:232:# CSS selector fails
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:233:node click.js --url https://example.com --selector ".btn-submit"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:234:# Error: waiting for selector ".btn-submit" failed
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:235:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:236:# Discover correct selector
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:237:node snapshot.js --url https://example.com | jq '.elements[] | select(.tagName=="BUTTON")'
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:238:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:239:# Try XPath
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:240:node click.js --url https://example.com --selector "//button[contains(text(),'Submit')]"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:241:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:242:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:243:### Common Mistakes
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:244:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:245:❌ Wrong working directory → output files go to wrong location
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:246:❌ Skipping output validation → silent failures
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:247:❌ Using complex CSS selectors without testing → selector errors
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:248:❌ Not checking element visibility → timeout errors
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:249:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:250:✅ Always verify `pwd` before running scripts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:251:✅ Always validate output after screenshots
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:252:✅ Use snapshot.js to discover selectors
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:253:✅ Test selectors with simple commands first
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:254:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:255:## Common Workflows
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:256:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:257:### Web Scraping
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:258:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:259:node evaluate.js --url https://example.com --script "
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:260:  Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.item')).map(el => ({
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:261:    title: el.querySelector('h2')?.textContent,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:262:    link: el.querySelector('a')?.href
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:263:  }))
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:264:" | jq '.result'
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:265:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:266:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:267:### Performance Testing
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:268:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:269:PERF=$(node performance.js --url https://example.com)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:270:LCP=$(echo $PERF | jq '.vitals.LCP')
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:271:if (( $(echo "$LCP < 2500" | bc -l) )); then
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:272:  echo "✓ LCP passed: ${LCP}ms"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:273:else
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:274:  echo "✗ LCP failed: ${LCP}ms"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:275:fi
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:276:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:277:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:278:### Form Automation
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:279:```bash
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:280:node fill.js --url https://example.com --selector "#search" --value "query" --close false
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/qa-closeout-3.log:281:node click.js --selector "button[type=submit]"
