_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:522:# P0-C architecture decision: inspection controller + route tree
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:523:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:524:Decision leg for `DIRECTION.md` V4. Read against `$H/02_EXPERIENCE_SPEC.md` §13,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:525:`$H/03_NAVIGATION_AND_STATE_CONTRACT.md` (all sections), `$H/04_COMPONENTS_AND_ASSETS.md`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:526:`$H/contracts/types.ts`, `$H/prototype/controller.js`, and the current
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:527:`src/layouts/{BaseLayout,PostLayout}.astro`, `src/pages/essays/[...slug].astro`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:528:`src/data/threads.ts`, `src/content.config.ts`, and `src/components/content/{Figure,PostSidebar,ThreadRail,ThreadBeat,ThreadStoryboard}.astro`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:529:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:530:**Correction to this leg's own brief, stated plainly before the decision:** the brief and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:531:`$H/03_*` both assert "`BaseLayout` uses Astro `ClientRouter`." That is false for the current
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:532:codebase. `grep -r ClientRouter src` returns zero hits outside this handoff's own docs;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:533:`BaseLayout.astro` renders no `<ClientRouter />`/`<ViewTransitions />` component, and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:534:`astro.config.mjs` sets no `output`/router config. The `astro:page-load` /
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:535:`astro:after-swap` listeners scattered across `Figure.astro`, `PostSidebar.astro`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:536:`ThreadRail.astro`, the card components, etc. are defensive (`astro:page-load` also fires
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:537:once on ordinary first load, ClientRouter or not) — they are not evidence ClientRouter is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:538:wired. The site today does plain multi-page navigation. This doesn't change which option
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:539:V4 asks for choosing between — it just means the choice is easier than the brief implies,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:540:because there is no live ClientRouter lifecycle to integrate with in the first place.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:541:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:542:## 1. Decision
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:543:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:544:**Own history directly for this reader route group; do not integrate with Astro
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:545:ClientRouter.** The essay route, the three new focus routes, and the figure route are
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:546:ordinary Astro static pages navigated with plain `<a href>` links (full page loads). Layered
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:547:on top, one `FocusHost` script per page manages `history.pushState`/`replaceState` and a
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:548:`popstate` listener under a private `rwFocus` state key — mirroring `$H/prototype/controller.js`'s
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:549:design (per V11) — to drive the in-place overlay. No `astro:page-load`/`astro:before-swap`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:550:hooks are added for this feature.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:551:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:552:**Why:** `$H/02_*`§13 and `$H/03_*`§4 both state this is the *default* recommendation for
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:553:reading routes regardless of what the rest of the site does, and integrating a second
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:554:navigation model would only be forced if ClientRouter were actually present and mandatory
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:555:site-wide — it isn't. Building this feature against a router that doesn't exist is premature
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:556:coupling: it would require inventing lifecycle-adapter code today for a hazard (two competing
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:557:`popstate` owners) that the current codebase cannot produce, and it would need redoing anyway
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:558:if ClientRouter is ever adopted, since that adoption is its own project with its own lifecycle
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:559:contract. Plain multi-page navigation is also what makes N06/N07/N09 (direct URL, refresh,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:560:no-JS) trivially true by construction rather than something the controller has to simulate.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:561:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:562:## 2. Route tree
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:563:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:564:All four routes are `getStaticPaths`-driven static pages (project default `output` is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:565:`'static'`; no adapter is configured) and each renders full content without JS, per V4/N09.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:566:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:567:| Route | File (new unless noted) | `getStaticPaths` source |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:568:|---|---|---|
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:569:| `/essays/<slug>/` | `src/pages/essays/[...slug].astro` (existing, unchanged) | `getCollection('posts')` |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:570:| `/essays/<slug>/thread/<beat>/` | `src/pages/essays/[slug]/thread/[beat].astro` | Cross product of `getCollection('posts')` filtered to posts with a `threads[post.id]` record, × that thread's `beats` (from `src/data/threads.ts`) |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:571:| `/essays/<slug>/evidence/` | `src/pages/essays/[slug]/evidence/index.astro` | One entry per post with an evidence set — `Object.values(evidence).filter(r => r.relatedSceneIds includes a beat of threads[post.id])` |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:572:| `/evidence/<record>/` | `src/pages/evidence/[record].astro` | One entry per record in `src/data/evidence.ts` (flat, **not** post-scoped — see §4) |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:573:| `/essays/<slug>/figure/<id>/` | `src/pages/essays/[slug]/figure/[id].astro` | Cross product of posts with a thread × that thread's beat ids; figure id === beat id for the six canonical scenes. The two closing figures (before/after estate, deep estate) are **not** routed — V8 keeps them in the closing sequence, never an expandable |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:574:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:575:`/evidence/<record>/` is deliberately top-level, not nested under `/essays/<slug>/`, because
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:576:evidence records are a site-wide resource per V13 (a second essay's receipts should be able
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:577:to reuse a record without a URL implying essay ownership); `/essays/<slug>/evidence/` is the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:578:essay-scoped index into that same flat set. **Risk:** verify neither new top-level segment
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:579:(`evidence`, and `essays/[slug]/*` alongside the existing `essays/[...slug]`) collides with
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:580:Astro's route-matching before P0-B builds it — `$H` flags this explicitly and it hasn't been
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:581:checked here.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:582:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:583:Each of the four new page files renders the *same* shared component (`ThreadFocus.astro`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:584:`EvidenceFocus.astro`, `FigureViewer.astro` — see §3) that also gets rendered inline into the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:585:essay page's `<template>` fragments. One renderer, two mount points; never a second
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:586:hand-written view.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:587:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:588:## 3. Dialog host design
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:589:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:590:One `FocusHost` Astro component, mounted once by `PostLayout` (and by the four new route
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:591:files, so a direct arrival at e.g. `/essays/x/thread/incident/` still has a working host if the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:592:reader then opens a *child* view — evidence or figure — from there). It owns:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:593:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:594:- **One `<dialog>` element**, opened with native `showModal()` — the same primitive
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:595:  `Figure.astro`'s existing private lightbox already uses, so there's one focus-trap/Escape/
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:596:  backdrop mechanism in the codebase, not two competing ones (see §5, risk 3).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:597:- **Content source: inline `<template>` fragments, not a client fetch.** Since the site is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:598:  static (no SSR endpoint to ask for a fragment at runtime, and no wish to hand-roll one),
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:599:  `PostLayout` renders `ThreadFocus`/`EvidenceFocus`/`FigureViewer` once per relevant id
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:600:  *inline on the essay page itself*, each wrapped in `<template data-focus-view="thread:incident">`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:601:  etc. — real server-rendered Astro output, not a JS string literal (the prototype's
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:602:  `window.RW_DATA.views` object was the same idea, done by hand; `<template>` is Astro's
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:603:  native equivalent and isn't parsed/fetched until cloned). `FocusHost.open(kind, id)` clones
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:604:  the matching template into the dialog and shows it. This is what lets the exact same
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:605:  component author both the standalone route and the overlay content with no second
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:606:  explanation (V3).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:607:- **Logical parent stack**, not nested DOM dialogs: an in-memory `Map<key, {kind, id,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:608:  parentKey, scrollTop, focusTargetId}>` plus a `currentKey`/`rootKey`, structurally the same
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:609:  shape as `controller.js`'s `entries` map (reused as reference per V11, rewritten in
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:610:  TypeScript — the prototype's Georgia/dark-only markup and CSS are not carried over). Opening
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:611:  evidence or a figure *from* Thread Focus pushes a child entry under the current thread key
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:612:  rather than replacing the dialog's whole state; closing one level pops to `parentKey`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:613:- **History**: one entry point locks the root (`replaceState` on first open, capturing scroll
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:614:  position under `rwFocus.key`), each subsequent open/swap `pushState`s or `replaceState`s a
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:615:  child key, and one `popstate` listener reconciles `history.state.rwFocus` back to the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:616:  matching map entry (or calls `restoreRoot()` if the key is the root / unknown). This is the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:617:  transition table in `$H/03_*`§3 implemented directly, not paraphrased.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:618:- **Focus containment/restoration** (V4, `$H/03_*`§5–6): capture `document.activeElement` and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:619:  scroll `{x,y}` before the first open; on full close, restore scroll then
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:620:  `.focus({preventScroll:true})` on the original trigger, falling back to the nearest heading
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:621:  and then the article `h1` if the trigger no longer exists. Tab stays inside the open
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:622:  `<dialog>` for free via `showModal()`; a programmatically-focusable title inside the cloned
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:623:  template receives initial focus, never a giant `aria-describedby` wrapper.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:624:- **Return semantics kept distinct** (N11): "Back to essay" always calls the full-chain close
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:625:  (`closeAll` → `restoreRoot`, original scroll position); "Read this scene in the essay" closes
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:626:  the chain and then does an explicit `scrollIntoView` + focus on `#thread-<beatId>` — a
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:627:  different, deliberate destination, never the old scroll position.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:628:- **No-JS / modifier-click safety**: every trigger (`data-kind`/`data-key` on an `<a href="/essays/.../thread/incident/">`)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:629:  is a real link to the standalone route first; the host's click handler only hijacks
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:630:  unmodified primary clicks (`!ctrlKey && !metaKey && !shiftKey && !altKey && button===0`),
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:631:  matching the prototype's guard. If `history.pushState` throws (storage/navigation
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:632:  unavailable), the host degrades to letting the real `href` fire rather than trapping the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:633:  reader in a half-open dialog (N10).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:634:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:635:## 4. Data contracts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:636:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:637:**`src/data/threads.ts`** is rewritten, not extended: beat order reverts to the canonical six
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:638:(`incident`, `deployment`, `use`, `drift`, `detection`, `outcome` — today's file has the wrong
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:639:six: `incident, divergence, detection, reconcile, use, outcome`). Each `ThreadBeat` record
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:640:gains the fields V3/V12 require so inline and focus rendering share one paragraph: `kind`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:641:(`historical | conceptual | mechanism | proposed`, from `$H/contracts/thread-manifest.json`'s
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:642:`mode`), `establishes: string`, `doesNotEstablish: string`, `longDescription: string`, and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:643:`relatedEvidenceIds: string[]` (post-scoped strings — see the risk below, not the contract's
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:644:`BeatId[]`). `recap` stays as the one real paragraph both `ThreadScene` (inline) and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:645:`ThreadFocus` (route/dialog) render — neither writes its own version.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:646:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:647:**`src/data/evidence.ts`** is new: a flat `Record<string, EvidenceRecord>`, seeded from
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:648:`$H/contracts/evidence-records.json` per V9 but reshaped to the fuller field set in
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:649:`02_EXPERIENCE_SPEC.md`§8 / `contracts/types.ts`'s `PublicEvidenceRecord` (id, title,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:650:evidenceClass, captureType, sourceUrl, sourceRevision, eventDate, recordedDate, verifiedAt,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:651:supports, limitations, publicability, relatedSceneIds, publicCapturePath) — reuse that
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:652:interface directly rather than reinventing a shape, widening `relatedSceneIds` from the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:653:contract's `BeatId[]` to `string[]` (see risk list, §6) so a second post's thread can
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:654:reference it later without a type change. P0-A re-grounds each record against the manuscript's
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:655:actual receipts before this file is written; this leg only fixes its shape.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:656:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:657:**Consumption, one path each:**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:658:- Inline: `ThreadScene.astro` (new — see §5) imports `threads`, looks up its own beat by
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:659:  `slug`+`beatId`, renders figure + `recap` + status label + an "Explore thread" link to
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:660:  `/essays/<slug>/thread/<beatId>/`, optionally with a `ReceiptDisclosure` for any
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:661:  `relatedEvidenceIds`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:662:- Route + overlay: `ThreadFocus.astro` does the same lookup and renders the fuller
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:663:  composition (heading, kind label, `recap`, figure, establishes/does-not, `RunningExampleCard`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:664:  `ThreadOverview`). It is invoked twice per essay build — once by
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:665:  `pages/essays/[slug]/thread/[beat].astro` for the standalone route, once inside a
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:666:  `<template>` on the essay page itself for the overlay (§3) — same component, same props,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:667:  zero forked copy.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:668:- `EvidenceFocus.astro` and `FigureViewer.astro` follow the identical two-mount-point pattern
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:669:  against `evidence.ts` and `threads.ts` respectively.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:670:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:671:## 5. Component reuse vs. replacement
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:672:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:673:| Component | Disposition | Why |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:674:|---|---|---|
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:675:| `ThreadStoryboard.astro` | **Delete.** Confirmed unwired: not imported by the essay MDX, `PostLayout`, or any page — only self-referenced and mentioned in comments elsewhere. | V3 |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:676:| `ThreadBeat.astro` | **Delete.** `grep -rl ThreadBeat src/content` returns only this essay's MDX, and every one of its six call sites uses the default `card` variant (none pass `variant="marker"`) — no other post uses either variant. | V3 ("keep only if grepped reuse elsewhere" — there is none) |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:677:| `ThreadRail.astro` | **Retired as a file; its beat-list markup, active-state styling, and `computeListWindow` windowing logic port into a new `ThreadDock.astro`** inside `ReadingCompanion`. Its current coupling to `ThreadStoryboard`'s `beatchange` CustomEvent is dropped (that emitter is deleted) — `ThreadDock`'s active-beat state instead comes from the same section/scene observer `SectionMarker` needs (V6), one observer, not two. | V3, V5 |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:678:| `PostSidebar.astro` | **Refactored, not deleted, into `ReadingCompanion.astro`.** Same sticky-column ownership role, rebuilt to the three-slot contract (nearby outline + `ThreadDock` + ≤1 `ContextualNote`) instead of today's takeaway-card/author-card/TOC/accordion. The `takeawayPlacement` frontmatter field and its `showRailTakeaway` branch in `PostLayout.astro` are removed with it, since `ExecutiveSignal` now always sits in-flow at entry (V5). | V5 |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:679:| `Figure.astro` | **Props kept unchanged** (`variant`/`width`/`height`/`longDescription`/etc.). Its *own* private `<dialog class="figure-lightbox">` (lines ~150–205) stays as the default for every ordinary figure elsewhere on the site — untouched, so other posts render unchanged (V13). Only when a new `figureId` prop is supplied does `expandable` route the trigger to `FocusHost` (`href="/essays/<slug>/figure/<id>/"`, `data-kind="figure" data-key="<id>"`) instead of opening its private dialog. This is what makes V7 additive rather than a sitewide `Figure` migration. | V7, V13 |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:680:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:681:## 6. Risks for P0-B/P0-C to watch
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:682:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:683:1. **Route collision** — confirm `/evidence/<record>/` and `/essays/[slug]/*` don't collide
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:684:   with the existing `src/pages/essays/[...slug].astro` catch-all before writing the four new
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:685:   page files; unchecked in this leg (per `$H`'s own instruction).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:686:2. **`relatedSceneIds`/`relatedEvidenceIds` typed too narrowly.** `contracts/types.ts`'s
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:687:   `BeatId` is a hardcoded six-value enum for this one thread. Ship `evidence.ts` and the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:688:   `threads.ts` extension with `string[]`, or V13's "site-wide capability, first consumer
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:689:   here" is false the moment a second essay gets a thread.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:690:3. **Two dialog mechanisms on one page.** `Figure.astro`'s private lightbox and `FocusHost`'s
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:691:   shared dialog must never both be open at once on the essay page. `FocusHost.open()` should
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:692:   close any open `[data-figure-dialog]` before showing its own, as a hard invariant, not an
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:693:   assumption.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:694:4. **Template payload weight.** Inlining `ThreadFocus`×6 + `EvidenceFocus` + `FigureViewer`×6
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:695:   as `<template>` fragments on every essay page adds real HTML weight even though templates
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:696:   aren't parsed until cloned — watch page size at the V04 "real manuscript density" QA gate,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:697:   and make sure images inside templates stay `loading="lazy"`/not preloaded.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:698:5. **Dead `astro:page-load` listeners.** Deleting `ThreadRail.astro`/`ThreadStoryboard.astro`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:699:   must also remove their `document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', …)` registrations
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:700:   along with the files — they're harmless no-ops once unmounted, not a correctness bug, but
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:701:   leaving them is a tell that the delete was partial.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:702:6. **No-JS audit is per-control, not visual.** N09 passes only if every "Explore thread" /
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:703:   "Read this scene" / evidence / figure trigger is a real `<a href>` to a working standalone
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:704:   route with JS off — check this by disabling JS per control at implementation time, not by
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:705:   eyeballing the rendered page.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:706:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:707:## Summary
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:708:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:709:The reading-route group navigates with plain Astro static pages and owns its own
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:710:`pushState`/`popstate` history directly, because Astro `ClientRouter` is not actually present
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:711:anywhere in this codebase today (the brief's premise was wrong) and both handoff documents
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:712:recommend exactly this as the default regardless; a `FocusHost` overlay clones pre-rendered
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:713:`<template>` fragments of the same `ThreadFocus`/`EvidenceFocus`/`FigureViewer` components that
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:714:back the four new static routes (`/essays/<slug>/thread/<beat>/`, `/essays/<slug>/evidence/`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:715:`/evidence/<record>/`, `/essays/<slug>/figure/<id>/`), so the overlay and the standalone pages
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:716:never diverge into two hand-written explanations. `ThreadStoryboard` and `ThreadBeat` are
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:717:confirmed dead/single-use and get deleted outright; `ThreadRail` and `PostSidebar` are
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:718:repurposed rather than replaced into `ThreadDock`/`ReadingCompanion`; `Figure.astro` gains an
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:719:opt-in `figureId` path into the shared overlay while keeping its existing private lightbox as
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:720:the untouched default everywhere else. The open risks that most need a second pair of eyes
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:721:before P0-B starts building are the unchecked route collision and the too-narrow `BeatId[]`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:722:typing that would quietly re-hardcode this as Registry-Wave-only.
