_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:732:## Method and evidence
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:733:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:734:`nvm use 22 && npm run build` (exit 0, 93 pages) → `npm run preview --port 4600`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:735:→ Playwright (Python, chromium) at desktop 1440x900 and mobile 390x844, light and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:736:dark theme forced via `localStorage['s2s-theme']` (the mechanism at
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:737:`src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro:97`). Screenshots and two capture logs are in this
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:738:directory. Computed styles and element counts were measured in-page rather than
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:739:inferred from source; where a claim rests on a measurement the number is quoted.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:740:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:741:⚠️ **Read this before trusting the first dark-theme screenshots.** Playwright
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:742:defaults to `prefers-color-scheme: light`. Finding **A1** below means that
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:743:default silently disabled every Tailwind `dark:` utility on the page. So the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:744:files named `*__desktop-dark.png` / `*__mobile-dark.png` show the site theme set
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:745:to dark **with `dark:` utilities inert** — which is a real reader state (any
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:746:reader on a light OS who picks the dark theme), but not the intended one. The
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:747:`*-dark-osdark.png` set (items 12-14) is the fair dark-theme render. `13b` is the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:748:deliberate A/B of the same region in the broken state. Judgments below are made
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:749:against the `osdark` set unless stated otherwise.
