_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:752:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:753:## A. Must-fix before P1
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:754:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:755:Ordered by leverage: A1 and A2 are each a handful of characters and each changes
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:756:how most of the page looks.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:757:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:758:### A1. Tailwind's `dark:` variant is bound to the OS media query, not the site's `.dark` class
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:759:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:760:**File:** `src/styles/global.css` (no `@custom-variant dark` declared anywhere in
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:761:the project — verified across `global.css`, `astro.config.mjs`; there is no
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:762:`tailwind.config.*`).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:763:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:764:**What's wrong.** Tailwind v4 compiles `dark:` into
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:765:`@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){…}` unless a custom variant says otherwise.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:766:Verified in the built CSS: `dist/_astro/BaseLayout.*.css` contains exactly one
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:767:`prefers-color-scheme` block, and 47+ `.dark\:…` utilities sit inside it. The
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:768:site's own theme is a `.dark` **class** on `<html>`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:769:(`BaseLayout.astro:36,97-105`). The two never meet. There are **370** `dark:`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:770:utilities in `src/`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:771:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:772:Measured proof, same element, site theme dark both times:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:773:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:774:| OS `prefers-color-scheme` | `[class*="bg-blue-50"]` computed background |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:775:|---|---|
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:776:| light | `oklch(0.97 0.014 254.604)` — i.e. `bg-blue-50`, near-white |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:777:| dark | `oklab(0.282 … / 0.3)` — i.e. `dark:bg-blue-950/30`, correct |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:778:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:779:**Reader-visible consequence.** Six `Callout` blocks on this essay
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:780:(`src/components/content/Callout.astro:34,42,50,58`) render as a near-white panel
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:781:while their contents keep dark-theme text tokens (`--text-secondary`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:782:`rgb(199,196,215)`). The "Evidence labels" callout wrapping `EvidenceLegend`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:783:(essay MDX line 406-407) is the worst case: light-grey body text on a white
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:784:panel, effectively unreadable. See
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:785:`06-conclusion-where-this-sits__desktop-dark.png` (broken) against
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:786:`13-callout-legend__desktop-dark-osdark.png` (correct).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:787:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:788:**What it should be.** V10: dark matches Tier A midnight/navy with restrained
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:789:violet structure, and theme is never hardcoded. Fix is one line —
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:790:`@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));` — after which all 370
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:791:utilities follow the user's choice.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:792:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:793:**Scope note:** this is pre-existing site-wide infrastructure, not something
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:794:P0-B/P0-C introduced. It is listed first anyway because until it is fixed, no
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:795:dark-theme fidelity judgment on this essay is trustworthy, and it is the cheapest
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:796:fix on this list.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:797:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:798:### A2. `--accent` is clobbered by a leftover shadcn HSL-triple block, so the violet accent never paints
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:799:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:800:**Files:** `src/styles/global.css:116` (`:root { --accent: #6366f1 }`) and `:170`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:801:(`.dark { --accent: #c0c1ff }`) — the real editorial accent — are both overridden
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:802:later in the same file at equal specificity by `:1770` (`:root { --accent: 210
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:803:40% 96.1% }`) and `:1792` (`.dark { --accent: 217.2 32.6% 17.5% }`).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:804:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:805:**What's wrong.** Those later values are shadcn-style raw HSL triples intended
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:806:for `hsl(var(--accent))`. Used directly as a colour they are invalid, so the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:807:declaration is dropped and the element falls back to inherited colour. Measured
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:808:on `.reading-companion__header`: the token resolves to `217.2 32.6% 17.5%` and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:809:the computed `color` is `rgb(218,226,253)` — that is `--text-primary`, not an
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:810:accent. **19** live elements on the essay page ask for `var(--accent)` as a
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:811:colour; 29 `text-[var(--accent)]` usages exist across `src/components` and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:812:`src/layouts`, plus ~8 `color: var(--accent)` rules inside `global.css` itself
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:813:(`:334, :491, :509, :576, :621`).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:814:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:815:Also `src/layouts/PostLayout.astro:106` — the reading-progress bar is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:816:`bg-[var(--accent)]`, so it paints no background at all and the progress
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:817:indicator is invisible.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:818:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:819:**What it should be.** Tier A 01/02/03 use violet consistently for the eyebrow
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:820:("EXECUTIVE SIGNAL", "READING COMPANION"), the active outline bullet and the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:821:section rule. Today only the components reaching for the *other* accent tokens
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:822:(`--accent-subtle`, `--accent-text`, `--cyan` — all real hex) show colour, which
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:823:is why "RUNNING EXAMPLE" is violet but "ON THIS PAGE" is near-white in
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:824:`01-entry__desktop-dark.png`. Delete or namespace the `:1756`/`:1779` block.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:825:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:826:### A3. `ReadingCompanion` never actually sticks — the rail is absent for ~90% of the essay
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:827:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:828:**Files:** `src/layouts/PostLayout.astro:211` (`xl:self-start` on the rail
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:829:column) and `:125` (`items-start` on the `.post-layout` grid); the sticky wrapper
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:830:is `:215`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:831:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:832:**What's wrong.** The wrapper's computed style *is* `position: sticky; top: 96px`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:833:but `align-self: start` makes the grid item exactly as tall as its own content,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:834:so the sticky element has no travel inside its containing block and cannot pin.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:835:Measured: companion rect `top` goes 457 → -402 across 859px of scroll — a 1:1
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:836:move, i.e. no pinning at all — and it is fully off-screen (`bottom: -1473`) by
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:837:`scrollY ≈ 2462`, while `.post-layout` is **23306px** tall.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:838:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:839:**Reader-visible consequence.** `02-threadscene-incident__desktop-dark.png`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:840:shows the entire right column empty at reading depth.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:841:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:842:**What it should be.** V5 and `IMAGE-GUIDE.md` §7 item 3: "Reading Companion is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:843:the only sticky essay sidebar surface at depth." Tier A 02 and 08 both show it
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:844:pinned beside mid-essay and conclusion content. The grid item needs to stretch to
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:845:the row height (`xl:self-stretch`, or drop `xl:self-start` given the column
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:846:already spans both rows) so the sticky child has somewhere to travel.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:847:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:848:### A4. Evidence Focus is unreachable from the essay — every evidence link is inside a `<template>`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:849:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:850:**Files:** `src/components/content/FocusTemplates.astro` (emits the fragments),
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:851:`src/content/posts/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain.mdx` (no
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:852:evidence entry point), `src/components/content/ReceiptDisclosure.astro` (built,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:853:imported by nothing).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:854:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:855:**What's wrong.** Measured two independent ways. Static: stripping
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:856:`<template>…</template>` from the built essay HTML leaves **0** of 24
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:857:`/evidence/<record>/` links and **0** of 5 `/essays/<slug>/evidence/` links.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:858:Live DOM at all four viewport/theme combinations: `evidenceLinks_live: 0`. The
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:859:`FocusHost` pathname interception works correctly (`src/lib/focus-host.ts:74-78`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:860:handles both evidence shapes), but there is no anchor on the page for a reader to
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:861:click. `grep -rln ReceiptDisclosure src` returns only the component file, and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:862:`claim-badge` appears 0 times in the built output.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:863:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:864:**What it should be.** V9: "The essay keeps a concise 'Receipts behind the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:865:argument' section with `ReceiptDisclosure` summaries; Evidence Focus holds the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:866:full set." `IMAGE-GUIDE.md` §7 items 9-10 both presume the reader can get there.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:867:Needs a real in-flow entry point in the MDX (and/or a rail slot) that links to
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:868:`/essays/<slug>/evidence/`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:869:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:870:### A5. Section markers (V6) do not exist
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:871:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:872:**Files:** no `SectionMarker` component exists — `ls src/components/content/`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:873:has no match for `section`/`marker`, and `grep -rln SectionMarker src` is empty.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:874:Heading rendering is plain `prose-custom` (`PostLayout.astro:249`).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:875:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:876:**What's wrong.** Measured on the essay page: `[class*="section-marker"],
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:877:[data-section-marker]` → **0** elements; `[aria-current="location"]` → **0**.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:878:There is no ordinal, no reserved-width left rule, and no active state.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:879:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:880:**What it should be.** V6 and spec §5: ordinal plus reserved-width left rule,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:881:exactly one active with the violet accent, `aria-current="location"` in the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:882:outline, observer- or rAF-driven, no history pushes. Tier A 02 shows the ordinal
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:883:in a bordered box (`01`) beside an eyebrow (`THE STALE REVIEWER · 1 OF 6`); Tier
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:884:A 03 shows the active violet rule running the section's full height; Tier A 08
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:885:shows `11 / CONCLUSION`. This is the most visible piece of missing editorial
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:886:furniture in the static shell — every section currently starts with bare prose
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:887:(`02-threadscene-incident__desktop-dark.png`,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:888:`06-conclusion-where-this-sits__desktop-dark.png`).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:889:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:890:Reserved-width matters: `IMAGE-GUIDE.md` §7 item 4 requires the active treatment
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:891:"without layout shift", so the gutter must be reserved whether or not the marker
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:892:is active.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:893:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:894:*Scope honesty:* `DIRECTION.md`'s package list assigns "active-section styling"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:895:to **P1**. The static ordinal/eyebrow/gutter is P0-B composition and is what
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:896:makes Tier A 02/03 legible as an editorial page, so it belongs here; the active
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:897:observer can land in P1 as planned.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:898:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:899:### A6. The frontispiece hero is not enabled, so entry does not match Tier A 01
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:900:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:901:**Files:** `src/content/posts/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain.mdx`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:902:frontmatter (lines 16-17 set `heroImage`/`heroAlt` but **no** `heroPlacement`);
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:903:mechanism at `src/layouts/PostLayout.astro:71,74,117-123`;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:904:schema at `src/content.config.ts:41`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:905:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:906:**What's wrong.** `heroPlacement` defaults to `'default'`, so `isFrontispiece` is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:907:false and the hero renders in the body column below the header
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:908:(`PostLayout.astro:229-237`). Measured: `h1` at y=159, hero plate at y=552 — the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:909:title comes first. Tier A 01 opens with the illustration above the breadcrumb and
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:910:title, with an overlaid `Editorial illustration • not a product screenshot`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:911:caption strip. `DIRECTION.md`'s reconciliation table is explicit: "frontispiece
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:912:hero stays (spec §4 Entry)". One frontmatter line.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:913:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:914:**Latent bug the flip will expose.** `PostLayout.astro:119` wraps the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:915:frontispiece in `max-w-[var(--measure)]`, but that div sits **outside**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:916:`article.post-layout` and `--measure` is defined only on `.post-layout`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:917:(`global.css:409,414`). Verified: the only element resolving `--measure` today is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:918:`.post-layout` itself (84ch → 1280px at xl). So the frontispiece wrapper's
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:919:`max-width` would be invalid and dropped, leaving it full-viewport-width below
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:920:1280px while the article body stays at 72-84ch. Fix both together.
