_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:950:`/evidence/<slug>/` renders them well (`10-evidence-record-route-full__desktop-dark.png`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:951:— honest "Not stated" values, "WHAT THIS SUPPORTS", "LIMITS", and a correct
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:952:"No standalone capture asset is published for this record" note). The data exists;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:953:the index does not use it.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:954:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:955:**What it should be.** Tier A 05 makes Evidence Focus itself a full receipt
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:956:surface — `RECEIPT SUMMARY` card with title, date, claim badge, the two-column
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:957:supported-claim / limitations split — with the index in the rail. At minimum this
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:958:route needs its own `h1` and the selected receipt rendered in full.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:959:
