_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:964:### A9. Figures render as a near-white slab in dark theme
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:965:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:966:**File:** `src/styles/global.css:830-832` — `.dark .figure-plate { background:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:967:#f3f5fa; }` (light value `:822` is `#f6f8fb`).
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:968:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:969:**What's wrong.** This is a real `.dark` class rule, so unlike A1 it is
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:970:deliberate, not a cascade accident — which is why it is phrased as a design
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:971:decision to revisit rather than a defect. Measured: **15** `.figure-plate`
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:972:elements on the essay page, all computing `rgb(243,245,250)` in dark theme. In
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:973:`14-threadscene__desktop-dark-osdark.png` the plate is the brightest object on
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:974:the page and outweighs the prose around it; the hero gets the same treatment plus
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:975:corner brackets at entry.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:976:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:977:**What it should be.** Tier A 02 and 04 mount figures in a **dark navy bordered
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:978:panel** whose header row reads `FIGURE 01 · DEPLOYMENT GAP` with `Enlarge figure
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:979:↗` at the right, caption in muted text at the bottom — the artwork stays light,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:980:the container does not. Tier A 01's hero bleeds to the pane edges with a caption
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:981:overlay and no plate or brackets at all. Since the thread PNGs are cream-toned,
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:982:the intent of a light mount is understandable; it is the *container*, not the
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:983:artwork, that should go dark.
