_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1049:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1050:# Route-backed inspection and return-state contract
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1051:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1052:## 1. Two presentations, one content record
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1053:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1054:A detail view has a real canonical route and a shared renderer. An ordinary in-essay click may render it in the overlay host while keeping the essay mounted. A copied link, direct arrival, refreshed deep URL, modifier click or no-JS visit renders the standalone route.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1055:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1056:Proposed routes (check collisions with the current Astro catch-all first):
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1057:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1058:```text
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1059:/essays/<post>/
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1060:/essays/<post>/threads/<thread>/<beat>/
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1061:/essays/<post>/evidence/
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1062:/essays/<post>/evidence/<receipt>/
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1063:/essays/<post>/figures/<figure>/
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1064:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1065:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1066:Prototype equivalents are actual sibling HTML files such as `thread-use.html` and `evidence-drift-check.html`. They are not production route names. Every prototype detail page includes static content, not a JavaScript-only empty shell.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1067:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1068:Never put return scroll coordinates or private source data into a public share URL. A copy-link action gives the canonical standalone URL. The origin/return token is private session state, not authority or an authentication token.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1069:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1070:## 2. State dimensions
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1071:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1072:```ts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1073:type ReaderLocation = { sectionId: string; sceneId: string | null };
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1074:type PreviewState = { heldSceneId: string | null; dockChoice: 'auto'|'open'|'closed' };
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1075:type FocusView = { kind: 'thread'|'evidence'|'figure'|'contents'; id: string };
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1076:type ReturnSnapshot = {
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1077:  entryKey: string; url: string; articleRevision: string;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1078:  x: number; y: number;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1079:  anchorId: string | null; offsetWithinAnchor: number;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1080:  focusTargetId: string | null;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1081:  openDisclosureIds: string[];
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1082:  reader: ReaderLocation; preview: PreviewState;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1083:  dismissedNoteIds: string[];
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1084:};
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1085:```
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1086:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1087:Reading position, dock preview, focus selection and browser navigation are **not one variable**. The user can read Drift while holding Use; opening a focus view does not move the underlying essay to that preview.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1088:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1089:## 3. Transition table
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1090:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1091:| Action | Document | History | Return behavior |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1092:|---|---|---|---|
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1093:| Scroll article | Update section rule/outline/context only | No push | No focus move |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1094:| Open Thread from essay | Preserve essay DOM; show Thread Focus | Push one owned detail entry | Root snapshot captured before lock |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1095:| Select another beat within modal | Replace focused content only | Replace owned detail entry | Original essay snapshot unchanged |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1096:| Open Evidence from Thread | Same dialog host, child logical state | Push child entry | Parent beat, pane scroll, disclosures retained |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1097:| Open Figure from Thread/Evidence | Same dialog host, figure state | Push child entry | Returns to immediate parent, not top of essay |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1098:| Escape / close current view | Remove one logical level | Back only within verified owned history | Restore parent; root if no parent |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1099:| Back to essay | Exit complete owned inspection chain | Traverse known owned depth only | Original snapshot, not selected beat anchor |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1100:| Read this scene in essay | Close focus then deliberate jump | Explicit anchor navigation | Chosen scene, not old reading point |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1101:| Browser Back / Forward | Reconcile with owned entries | No extra push | Reopen corresponding view or restore root |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1102:| Copy/open direct detail URL | Standalone server-rendered page | Ordinary navigation | “Read in essay” to related anchor |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1103:| Refresh on detail URL | Standalone page | Keep URL | No claim that a mounted background survives |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1104:| JS/navigation failure | Follow real href or local dialog fallback | Do not trap user | Standard page/anchor remains reachable |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1105:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1106:## 4. History ownership
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1107:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1108:`pushState` changes the address/history but does not load the target resource. Therefore that URL must independently resolve on refresh. `pushState` and `replaceState` do not dispatch `popstate`; the controller must update its view directly on those operations and respond separately to browser traversal [MDN-01, MDN-02].
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1109:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1110:Merge namespaced state into `history.state`; do not replace unrelated application data. Include a per-document/session token and opaque entry keys. Never use `history.length > 1` as proof that Back is safe. Do not invoke `history.back()` or `history.go(-n)` unless the controller can demonstrate a contiguous chain of its own entries. Direct arrivals always get a deterministic “Read in essay” route instead.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1111:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1112:One controller owns this route group. Default recommendation: render reading routes without Astro ClientRouter and use normal links for entry/exit. Astro's ordinary default is full-page navigation [ASTRO-01]. This is a bounded choice for the reading routes, not a mandate to remove ClientRouter from the whole site.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1113:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1114:If the actual site requires ClientRouter on these routes, integration is a separate mandatory task: use router lifecycle/loader/swap hooks and one route state owner. Do not paste the standalone prototype controller alongside ClientRouter's `popstate` handler. Astro's `astro:after-swap` / `astro:page-load` lifecycle requires explicit setup and cleanup [ASTRO-01].
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1115:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1116:## 5. Return-position algorithm
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1117:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1118:1. Before opening: capture URL, x/y, nearest stable block anchor and relative offset, active element, disclosure states and reader preferences.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1119:2. Lock the background while preserving its exact DOM. Use tested body-scroll locking, not only an `overflow:hidden` assumption on iOS.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1120:3. Keep focus inside the active dialog. Suspend passive reading/context changes.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1121:4. On return to the same mounted document: restore body styles and original x/y; then focus the original trigger with `preventScroll`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1122:5. If content/viewport changed, prefer anchor + relative offset over an old pixel coordinate; clamp to document bounds. Wait for relevant layout-affecting images/fonts before final correction. Never smooth-scroll the entire article during restoration.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1123:6. If the trigger no longer exists, focus the related heading, then article heading as last fallback.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1124:7. On direct URL or refreshed document, render standalone. An optional session-backed “Resume saved position” may be added later only after matching origin/revision/entry and testing; it is not MVP behavior.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1125:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1126:Only one modal DOM node is open at a time. A logical parent stack is permitted. Store each parent's scroll and local expansion state before replacing the host. Restoring an evidence view must restore open receipts, not recreate a collapsed set at the top.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1127:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1128:## 6. Focus and interaction
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1129:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1130:Opening a substantial detail view focuses a programmatically focusable title near the start. No giant `aria-describedby` wrapping all structured content. Tab stays inside the modal. Escape and visible close are equivalent one-level return actions. A separate “Back to essay” exits the full inspection chain. For a direct route, there is no modal trap and no simulated prior reading state [W3C-01].
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1131:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1132:Opening a focus view from another focus view requires an explicit click. No automatic dialog from scrolling, no focus moves during reading, no auto-open receipt and no auto-swapping images. Backdrop clicks may close Figure Viewer; for full Thread/Evidence views, keep the default conservative (visible Close or Escape), avoiding accidental dismissal during reading.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1133:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1134:Preserve ordinary anchors and modifier semantics. `target="_blank"` is used only by explicitly labeled new-tab actions. Raw source/external links may follow the site's normal policy; opening a new tab is not the primary place-preservation strategy.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1135:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1136:## 7. Freshness, URLs and public data
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1137:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1138:Stable receipt IDs do not prove sources. Only source records populate public capture links. Sanitize before bundling content into HTML, JSON or static routes. A collapsed disclosure or modal is not access control. Do not ship internal IPs, credentials, private tracker IDs or unapproved raw logs in a hidden component.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1139:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1140:An inspection route represents one view of public content, not a new published essay. Define canonical links and metadata accordingly; use actual content type and relationship to parent. Do not manufacture a publication date merely because a route was generated. Check indexing policy with the site's owner.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1141:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1142:## 8. Prototype validation boundary
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1143:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1144:The current environment's browser policy blocked navigation to local HTTP and file URLs. Rendering and interaction checks use Chromium `set_content` on the supplied self-contained HTML. The prototype handles unavailable History API URL mutation by retaining an in-document dialog stack. This fallback was exercised; it is **not** a successful hosted Back/Forward test.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1145:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1146:Hosted route refresh, real URL traversal, browser Forward, Safari/iOS scroll restoration and ClientRouter integration remain mandatory local tests. The handoff includes their acceptance matrix rather than claiming they passed here.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1147:---
