_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1183:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1184:# Reading experience v2
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1185:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1186:## 1. Purpose
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1187:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1188:Provide one coherent, premium long-form reading experience, with optional depth that never loses the reader's place. Adopt the visual language selected from images 01–02: midnight/navy surfaces, restrained violet/cyan structure, editorial serif titles, clear sans-serif controls, and generous but bounded whitespace.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1189:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1190:**Read the essay. Inspect a thread. Check the evidence. Return exactly where you left.**
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1191:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1192:The problem is not insufficient functionality. It is ambiguous surface ownership: the old generated images mixed the article, an artifact inspector, an evidence library and a reader-navigation panel. This spec makes those contexts explicit.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1193:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1194:## 2. Scope and authority
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1195:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1196:Owner: Signal to System; canonical portfolio layer: GTM and Communication. Governance/Evaluation contributes evidence labels and clearance rules, not new runtime features. Agent postures: Editorial Architect, UX Implementer, Accessibility Reviewer, Evidence Reviewer. Current source of record: proposed GitHub design/implementation handoff. Optional rationale writeback: MeatyWiki after approval.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1197:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1198:This pass reviews the supplied artifacts and screenshots. It did **not** re-read the live repository or current local working tree. The v1 source pin `cc9f3ed…` is an inherited locator only. Agents must inspect their current layout, router, components, installed Astro version and lockfile before patching.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1199:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1200:Precedence: current user decisions → this v2 interaction contract → current manuscript/evidence/canonical artwork → v1 details not explicitly superseded → generated images for visual inspiration only. A source or current hand edit outranks prototype prose. Generated evidence is never an authority.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1201:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1202:## 3. Core concepts and modes
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1203:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1204:| Mode | Primary content | Right rail | Entry behavior |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1205:|---|---|---|---|
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1206:| Essay View | Title, prose, six inline scenes, tables, illustrative comparison, evidence summaries, actual closing figures and WhereThisSits | Entry: author + Executive Signal in flow. Reading: one sticky ReadingCompanion | Standard article route |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1207:| Thread Focus | One selected beat, its canonical figure, detailed interpretation, scope/limits and related evidence | **Only** RunningExampleCard + ThreadOverview | Modal from essay; standalone on direct link |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1208:| Evidence Focus | Receipt set or selected receipt; source, support, limits, actual capture where available | EvidenceGuide + ReceiptIndex | Modal from essay/thread; standalone on direct link |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1209:| Figure Viewer | One figure, exact caption, long description and relevant source/asset metadata | None | Same overlay host or standalone figure route |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1210:| Mobile Contents | Article outline and thread navigation | None; single-column sheet | User-triggered short sheet, not a chatbot |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1211:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1212:Author cards, Executive Signal, article TOC, decorative quotations and WhereThisSits do **not** appear in Thread Focus. Article TOC does not appear in Evidence Focus. A “Read in essay” action is enough context; the reader does not need the whole essay sidebar duplicated.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1213:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1214:## 4. Essay layout
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1215:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1216:### Main grid
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1217:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1218:Use a centered shell around 1320–1400px wide on large displays, with a 280–310px rail, 36–50px gap and remaining width allocated to the primary pane. Prose measure is approximately 65–72 characters, not the entire diagram width. At widths below roughly 980–1040px, remove the persistent rail and use Contents. Confirm breakpoints with real content, not device labels.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1219:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1220:The prototype uses Georgia and system sans-serif to avoid external dependencies. Production should reuse the approved site fonts. Do not distribute font binaries in the handoff.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1221:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1222:### Main-pane composition types
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1223:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1224:- **Measure:** ordinary Markdown paragraphs and headings. This remains the default.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1225:- **Pane:** detailed figures, taxonomy/comparison tables, and occasional major callouts.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1226:- **Split:** a defined prose block beside a compact illustrative card or note. Use CSS grid; stack when prose would become too narrow.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1227:- **Inset:** local aside, short definition or evidence caveat. No third global rail.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1228:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1229:“Full width” always means the primary pane's width, not the viewport and not across the sidebar. Do not crop a technical figure to fit a split. On small screens the explanation precedes the supporting visual in DOM order.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1230:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1231:### Entry
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1232:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1233:HeroFrontispiece → breadcrumb/category → title and deck → real publication/update/read-time data → reading-path chip/tags → slim RevisionNote → opening narrative. The hero is not a large modal or an auto-advancing banner. A separate mobile crop may be necessary; technical figures may not be cropped. Hero/social assets remain separate.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1234:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1235:The author and one Executive Signal sit beside the entry in flow. They do not reappear every time a section changes. On mobile, the author becomes a compact byline and Executive Signal is one short disclosure. A reduced header does not become a second repeated article title at every scene.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1236:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1237:RevisionNote defaults closed. Do not import the old generated “re-published” date or an invented read time. The prototype labels itself a layout review instead of creating publication metadata.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1238:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1239:## 5. SectionMarker and reading position
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1240:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1241:A section has a visible ordinal and a thin left rule spanning the defined section block. Inactive rules use the subtle border token. Exactly one current section rule uses violet. Keep its width reserved: changing from inactive to active must not move the prose.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1242:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1243:Use the same active section ID for the rule and the outline. Determine the active section from a stable reading line below the sticky header; handle reverse scrolling, tall sections, deep links and the bottom of the document. A single rAF-throttled scroll calculation or observer strategy is sufficient. Passive reading does not push history entries, mark sections “complete,” or announce every scroll event to a screen reader.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1244:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1245:The ordinal, heading and `aria-current="location"` on the relevant outline link provide non-color information. Keyboard focus remains a different visual state from reading position. Avoid animated height fills, multicolor chapter gamification or scroll-jacking.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1246:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1247:## 6. ReadingCompanion and ContextualNote
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1248:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1249:The one sticky reading companion contains:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1250:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1251:1. Compact nearby-chapter outline and an “All sections” action.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1252:2. ThreadDock, current when in a scene and labeled “Last thread scene” between scenes.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1253:3. **At most one** authored ContextualNote.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1254:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1255:When these cannot fit in the viewport, simplify or switch to flow; do not create nested scroll areas. The prototype compacts the outline and falls back to flow for an oversized companion.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1256:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1257:### ContextualNote contract
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1258:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1259:`ContextualNote` is a short, explicitly authored annotation keyed to `sectionId` or `sceneId`. It is not dynamically invented and makes no model call. It can explain a distinction, define a term, or note an evidence limit. Its expanded content should remain short; lengthy content belongs in the essay or Evidence Focus.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1260:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1261:Example mapping:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1262:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1263:| Location | Visible note | Optional expansion |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1264:|---|---|---|
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1265:| Artifact definition | **The runtime executes.** An artifact shapes behavior. | Why instruction presence does not establish compliance |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1266:| Deployment | **A copy has its own state.** | Source, binding, deployment and loading are distinct |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1267:| Managed variation | **Governed is not identical.** | Older is not automatically stale; difference is not approval |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1268:| Outcome | **Unknown is a valid state.** | Today's registry is not historical run attestation |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1269:| Receipts | **Read the limits with the finding.** | Summary versus original capture versus fresh measurement |
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1270:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1271:No note is required in every section. No blank card is reserved when none exists. “Dismiss” applies to that note ID for the current visit. “Collapse” applies to its detail; a dismissed note does not immediately reopen on another scroll event. Optionally offer a reader preference to hide all context notes.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1272:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1273:Switch notes only when the active semantic section changes, not at every paragraph or pixel. Pause replacement while focus is inside the note/companion or an overlay is open. Do not automatically expand a note. Mobile renders useful note content as an inline disclosure near the relevant text or under Contents—not floating over paragraphs.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1274:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1275:### ThreadDock contract
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1276:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1277:Manual collapse takes precedence over proximity-triggered expansion. Holding a beat pins the **preview**, not the physical page or actual reading position. Display both when different: “Held preview: Use · Reading: Drift.” Default follow mode updates only sidebar context. It must never swap the inline canonical figure or automatically scroll the article.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1278:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1279:“Explore thread” opens the focused inspector for the selected or current beat. Focus mode has its own selected beat; it does not move the essay underneath. Keep the names **Incident, Deployment, Use, Drift, Detection, Outcome**.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1280:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1281:## 7. Inline ThreadScene and focused ThreadStoryboard
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1282:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1283:The editorial thread is distributed through the essay. All six canonical images stay in order and next to their prose, per the image handoff. No interaction is required to understand the argument.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1284:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1285:The main-pane scene contains a small number/label, its real paragraph(s), a semantic-status label where necessary, the figure/caption, and an “Explore thread” link. Remove redundant recap cards that duplicate both prose and image.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1286:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1287:The same data record drives inline and focus rendering. Never maintain a separately rewritten explanation inside the focus view without a defined editorial owner.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1288:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1289:### Thread Focus composition
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1290:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1291:Use image 05's primary hierarchy: a clear beat heading, a small kind label, real explanatory text, a generous figure, and a compact “what this establishes / what it does not” section. Use image 04's artifact-card shape, but replace every invented field with verified metadata or omit it. Artifact ID is `task-completion-validator`; do not substitute `agent-router`, a generic “researcher,” an invented version, digest, environment or approval.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1292:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1293:Right rail, in order:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1294:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1295:- RunningExampleCard: title, artifact identity, role, verified scope and provenance; no health/approval badge inferred from a registry.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1296:- ThreadOverview: six real beat links, selected beat, and a brief explanation that this is an editorial sequence rather than six successive observed events.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1297:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1298:At top: Back to essay (in-place entry only), view label, Copy link, Close. “Read this scene in the essay” is separate: it deliberately jumps to the chosen beat instead of restoring the original reading position.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1299:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1300:Inside modal focus mode, previous/next beat replaces the focused-view history entry. It does not create six history items. Direct-route navigation remains ordinary links. Do not leave “Hold preview” in focus mode: the selected focus beat already stays stable until the reader changes it. Hold belongs only to the essay dock.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1301:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1302:### Semantic boundaries
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1303:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1304:T01/T02: historical account of corrected source/registry and distinct consumer copies. T03: conceptual branch assuming the corrected instruction is present; **instruction present ≠ instruction followed**. This is not a gateway/signature-bypass illustration. T04: explicit return to the original five-day discrepancy, not five fresh measurements. T05: dated mechanism/receipt reference whose event/receipt timing remains subject to existing source reconciliation. T06: proposed evidence linkage; no improved outcome or closed-loop implementation implied.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1305:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1306:## 8. Evidence Focus and receipts
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1307:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1308:Keep a concise “Receipts behind the argument” section inside the essay. A few disclosure summaries make key findings and limits visible; the reader should not have to inspect every receipt to understand the thesis.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1309:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1310:Evidence Focus provides the full record set. Each receipt includes:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1311:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1312:- stable ID and title;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1313:- evidence class;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1314:- event date, recorded date and verified date when independently known;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1315:- source locator and source revision when available;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1316:- the supported statement;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1317:- explicit limits/counter-evidence;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1318:- capture type: original, redacted capture, method summary, illustrative example or not applicable;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1319:- publicability status;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1320:- links to the relevant essay paragraphs and scenes.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1321:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1322:A method summary must not masquerade as raw output. A code-like panel is permitted for **actual supplied captures** or explicitly marked illustrative schemas, never a generated signature verifier presented as observed implementation. Missing source URL, commit or exact runtime identity stays missing. Do not invent `E-1023`, a plausible commit hash, an official report or a 90-day measured gain.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1323:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1324:Evidence label is not evidence quality. “Externally reported” means attributed, not validated by us. “Measured” requires a stated method and denominator; it does not automatically mean causal. “Implemented” is a separate maturity dimension, not a synonym for “Observed.” A green color alone may not collapse these distinctions.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1325:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1326:The prototype uses bounded manuscript method summaries, with their lack of primary captures shown in every record. No measured outcome improvement is included.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1327:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1328:### Routing and tabs
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1329:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1330:Open in-place on an ordinary click from the essay or thread. Each record has a canonical URL and an explicit “Open in new tab” link. Preserve Cmd/Ctrl-click, middle-click and context menu. No forced new-tab default. Direct arrivals see a standalone evidence page, with “Read in essay,” not “Your place is saved.”
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1331:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1332:## 9. Managed variation is inline, not another mode
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1333:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1334:Image 06 explains why three project states warrant different decisions. It is not a live deployment dashboard, a separate historical run or a Thread Focus page.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1335:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1336:Retain a single compact comparison in the actual managed-variation section. Compare against each intended binding: A needs update; B needs inspection/reconciliation of local changes; C matches a deliberate pin that remains conditional on applicable policy. The example is explicitly illustrative. Do not label a mandatory security patch as safely ignorable because a project is pinned.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1337:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1338:Prefer a responsive HTML comparison for this specific optional example. It does not replace the canonical thread or closing figures. Do not show the same three-way concept again in a neighboring full-width graphic unless the repetition adds distinct information.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1339:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1340:## 10. Figure Viewer
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1341:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1342:Use the successful frame from image 08: large image, title, caption, long description, close and copy-link actions. Content is the **exact** selected asset and its metadata. Never redraw a canonical image inside the viewer, advertise an SVG download for a PNG, or invent image dimensions.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1343:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1344:From the essay, Close/Escape/Back returns to its trigger at the same reading position. From Thread Focus, it returns to the same beat and focus-pane scroll position. Only one dialog is active. A logical parent stack replaces nested DOM dialogs. Optional previous/next figure controls remain within the related figure group; they never change the underlying essay's reading position.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1345:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1346:Use accessible dialog semantics, visible Close, focus containment and restoration. Long structured content gets a focusable heading rather than a giant `aria-describedby` paragraph [W3C-01]. Do not claim accessibility conformance from a screenshot.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1347:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1348:## 11. Closing and WhereThisSits
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1349:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1350:Closing sequence stays grounded in the current manuscript: concise receipts → latest estate before/after → latest deep estate figure → closing argument → WhereThisSits → sources. The deep estate image is the last architecture-heavy image. Missing actual assets reserve a labeled development slot, never publish a substitute city illustration.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1351:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1352:At the conclusion, the rail contains a compact final outline/next-question context, not the author biography, Executive Signal or an invented testimonial.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1353:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1354:WhereThisSits answers prior/current/next **questions across the guided reading path**. Ordinary SeriesBreadcrumb says where a page belongs within one actual series. The two share typography but not semantics. Use the actual five essays; the next relevant essay is The Contract Is the Work. Deterministic Envelope remains planned until its real publication record changes. Do not invent “Agentic Ecosystems and Real-World Adoption.”
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1355:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1356:## 12. Mobile
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1357:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1358:The visual language is achievable as responsive HTML/CSS. A native app or PWA is not required. Keep the hero crop, serif title, navy surfaces, touch-sized controls and bottom-sheet Contents treatment. Reject the mockup's fake Home/Library/Agents tab bar and AI assistant.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1359:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1360:Short navigation opens in a bottom sheet; long Thread/Evidence Focus uses the full viewport. A persistent top return control remains available. Use `100dvh` and safe-area padding; test dynamic browser chrome, orientation, on-screen keyboard, zoom and iOS scroll locking. Respect reduced motion. No automatic audio, parallax, swipe-only controls or interactions that require hover.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1361:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1362:The figure caption/textual explanation remains useful at mobile width. Technical art may require enlargement. Do not render all six raster labels at illegible size and call that responsive.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1363:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1364:## 13. Technical approach, integrations and MVP
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1365:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1366:Use shared Astro templates plus one small reader/focus controller. Ordinary prose, figures, receipts and tables remain server-rendered. Thread/Evidence/figure routes exist even without JavaScript. Static generation can enumerate records; verify the current route tree before adding patterns [ASTRO-02].
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1367:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1368:The in-place dialog and return-stack behavior is a custom enhancement, not a turnkey Astro feature. The recommended initial implementation uses native multi-page routes in this reader route group and **one owner for History API handling**. Do not run a second custom history/popstate loop concurrently with ClientRouter. If ClientRouter is mandatory globally, use an explicit lifecycle adapter and its tests or temporarily fall back to normal detail navigation [ASTRO-01].
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1369:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1370:MVP: consistent essay shell and component data → canonical standalone focus routes → in-place inspection with restoration → mobile/keyboard QA → visual refinements. Holding previews and sophisticated transition animation are secondary. Do not delay publication for a chat assistant, dashboard or animation subsystem.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1371:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1372:## 14. Success criteria
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1373:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1374:A successful implementation is readable with every disclosure closed, uses only approved technical art, keeps the original six-scene order, and lets the reader inspect depth without losing place. Thread Focus shows exactly the two approved sidebar components. Evidence Focus has no fabricated capture. Passive scroll changes orientation only. Direct links and no-JS routes work. Keyboard, Back/Forward and explicit return actions have documented, tested semantics. Final tests use the actual manuscript and artwork, not only this shorter representative content.
