_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1527:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1528:## Canonical page-state rules visible in Tier A
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1529:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1530:- **Essay View:** primary pane + sidebar. Author and Executive Signal are normal-flow entry components; deeper in the essay only Reading Companion remains sticky.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1531:- **Thread Focus:** focused inspection surface. Sidebar = Running Example + Thread Overview only. No author card, Executive Signal, or article TOC.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1532:- **Evidence Focus:** focused inspection surface. Sidebar = Evidence Guide + Receipt Index only.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1533:- **FigureViewer:** overlay/modal on top of the immediate prior context, and Close returns to that exact context.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1534:- **Managed Variation:** remains inline in the essay.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1535:- **WhereThisSits:** distinct from ordinary breadcrumb/series navigation; it explains the conceptual reading path.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1536:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1537:---
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1538:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1539:# 2. Rich component direction — Tier B
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1540:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1541:These are **secondary visual references**, deliberately retained because they often contain richer card/detail treatments than the canonical composite set.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1542:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1543:Use them for:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1544:- card depth, glow, icon sizing, borders, spacing, mini-diagram polish;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1545:- detailed Thread Overview and Running Example styling;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1546:- ReceiptDisclosure/evidence-card richness;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1547:- FigureViewer caption/control richness;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1548:- typographic rhythm inside a component.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1549:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1550:Do **not** use them to override:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1551:- which components appear in the sidebar at a given scroll depth;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1552:- whether something is a page versus a modal/focus surface;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1553:- essay/thread/evidence information architecture;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1554:- any factual copy, metrics, versions, availability states, or receipts;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1555:- the final mobile navigation model.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1556:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1557:### Files
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1558:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1559:- `01_essay-entry__rich-concept.png` — favored neo-editorial visual density and polish.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1560:- `02_first-scroll__rich-concept.png` — rich first-scroll / diagram treatment; sidebar hierarchy is superseded.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1561:- `03_artifact-partial-context__rich-concept.png` — detailed MediaSplit, table, badges; Executive Signal persistence is superseded.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1562:- `04_thread-deployment__rich-concept.png` — useful Running Example detail card and technical figure polish; use canonical Thread Focus composition instead.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1563:- `05_thread-use-overview__rich-concept.png` — strongest visual inspiration for Thread Overview / selected beat / hold state; canonical mode/sidebar rules supersede surrounding page.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1564:- `06_managed-variation__rich-concept.png` — strong visual language for the three-path comparison; canonical semantics and copy supersede it.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1565:- `07_evidence-receipts__rich-concept.png` — excellent Evidence/Receipt styling; **all fabricated receipt content is non-authoritative**.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1566:- `08_figure-viewer__rich-concept.png` — detailed FigureViewer controls, caption treatment, previous/next; canonical return-state contract supersedes unsupported controls.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1567:- `09_conclusion__rich-concept.png` — useful architecture-card treatment; invented next-essay and outcome copy must not be used.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1568:- `10_mobile__rich-concept.png` — visual inspiration for mobile surfaces; robot assistant/app-tab concepts are superseded.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1569:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1570:---
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1571:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1572:# 3. V2 prototype markups — Tier C
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1573:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1574:`03_V2_PROTOTYPE_MARKUPS/` is the rendered prototype family from the current experience specification. It is less visually lush than Tier B but is more trustworthy for **state and interaction semantics**.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1575:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1576:Use it to resolve questions like:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1577:- when the right rail changes;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1578:- how Contextual Notes collapse/expand;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1579:- what Thread Focus vs standalone thread looks like;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1580:- how Evidence Focus returns;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1581:- what mobile sheet/focus layouts do;
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1582:- how the thread sequence maps to essay anchors.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1583:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1584:If a Tier-A image is visually ambiguous, consult V2 markups and `06_SUPPORTING_HANDOFFS/CURRENT-EXPERIENCE-SPEC.md`.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1.log:1585:
