_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1-2.log:75:627:- `op day` owns human-authored daily framing; HAI transports human decisions; IntentTree tracks work; and portfolio-intelligence holds adjudicated roadmap/decision artifacts. None owns the long-horizon authority for “why this deserves time.” `node_01KZJ9YEC1RZVVP1Y89G6V17WY` records the missing charter/admission boundary. [Task 1]
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1-2.log:76:628-- The proposed layer is a concise direction charter, a small set of active commitments (purpose, outcome, duration, user role), admission with displacement, searchable incubation, and commitment-level review. Agents may draft proposals/evidence, but only the human activates/retires commitments, materially reinterprets purpose, admits projects, changes allocation, or accepts displacement. [Task 1]
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/p0d-p1-2.log:77:629-- Desired contract: the user supplies intent, ideas, direction, consequential decisions, and human-sovereign grants; Metis/agents own daily prioritization, orchestration, continuation, maintenance, recovery, validation, and delivery. A single attention card is reserved for matters unresolved by charter/policy/reversible default and includes recommendation, evidence, default, deadline, displacement, and consequence of silence. [Task 2]
