_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:31207: <Evidence kind="observed" /> **The reviewer copy.** The drift-check source records a deployed reviewer missing its mandatory establish-the-diff step while the upstream copy contained it. The incident was filed August 5; the check was committed August 6. Its five-day interval describes the stale deployment. Comparing deployed bytes with the source makes that discrepancy visible, but doesn't recover a per-session loading history or count incorrect reviews.[^drift]
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:31208: 
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:31209: <Evidence kind="observed" /> **Sibling instructions.** One harness-specific instruction file carried superseded doctrine for six weeks after its canonical sibling changed. The parity gate committed August 5 checks a declared relationship between those files. It doesn't require every document to be identical. The separate live-document staleness check catches a named obsolete assertion outside that pair; it leaves dated historical records alone.[^parity][^staleness]
