_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35258:dist/essays/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain/index.html-310-<p><em>A live run, redacted, September 15, 2026. The <span class="glossary-term"> <dfn tabindex="0" aria-describedby="glossary-tooltip-task-completion-validator">task-completion-validator</dfn> <span role="tooltip" id="glossary-tooltip-task-completion-validator" class="glossary-tooltip"> <span class="glossary-tooltip-definition">A reviewer that checks a claimed completion against what actually shipped, rather than trusting the report: it verifies the work is functional and meets its stated requirements before accepting it as done.</span>  </span> </span> drift this section describes is recorded in the receipt below (August 6, 2026), not replayed here; that nonzero exit is a different, unrelated undeclared-copy finding.</em></p>
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35259:dist/essays/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain/index.html-311-<aside class="lift-hover my-5 flex gap-4 rounded-xl border p-4 border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 dark:border-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-950/30" role="note"><div class="mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-blue-500 dark:text-blue-400" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4"></path><path d="M12 8h.01"></path></svg></div><div class="min-w-0 flex-1"><p class="mb-1 text-sm font-semibold text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-300">What this looks like in my lab</p><div class="prose prose-sm dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-inherit [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0"><p><strong>Implemented:</strong> SkillMeat manages artifact registration and deployment. The <span class="glossary-term"> <dfn tabindex="0" aria-describedby="glossary-tooltip-operator">Operator</dfn> <span role="tooltip" id="glossary-tooltip-operator" class="glossary-tooltip"> <span class="glossary-tooltip-definition">The work-routing surface that sits over the AOS subsystems: it takes an incoming idea or request, classifies it, and dispatches it to the right subsystem at the right effort level.</span>  </span> </span> sits over the subsystems. That is one implementation of coordination, not a requirement that enterprises adopt one router.</p><p><strong>Implemented:</strong> <span class="glossary-term"> <dfn tabindex="0" aria-describedby="glossary-tooltip-meatywiki">MeatyWiki</dfn> <span role="tooltip" id="glossary-tooltip-meatywiki" class="glossary-tooltip"> <span class="glossary-tooltip-definition">A durable knowledge store built on a file-first markdown vault: it compiles ingested material into structured, queryable knowledge that survives past any single session.</span>  </span> </span>, my durable knowledge store, and <span class="glossary-term"> <dfn tabindex="0" aria-describedby="glossary-tooltip-research-foundry">Research Foundry</dfn> <span role="tooltip" id="glossary-tooltip-research-foundry" class="glossary-tooltip"> <span class="glossary-tooltip-definition">An evidence-oriented research system: it runs research passes, extracts and verifies claims against sources, and produces evidence a reviewer can check instead of trusting recall.</span>  </span> </span>, my evidence-oriented research system, give context and evidence homes beyond the registry. <span class="glossary-term"> <dfn tabindex="0" aria-describedby="glossary-tooltip-meatyprompts">MeatyPrompts</dfn> <span role="tooltip" id="glossary-tooltip-meatyprompts" class="glossary-tooltip"> <span class="glossary-tooltip-definition">An earlier prompt-management experiment that preceded SkillMeat: a first attempt at giving reusable prompts a durable home instead of leaving them in one-off chat transcripts.</span>  </span> </span>, my earlier prompt-management experiment, was part of the path here.</p><p><strong>Proposed:</strong> complete cross-system linkage from loaded artifact version to accepted outcome. Local checks are implemented; fleet-wide compliance remains a target state in the registry’s own August 11 rules.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-coverage" id="user-content-fnref-coverage" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">19</a></sup></p><p><strong>Proposed:</strong> controlled comparisons of pinned artifacts and context are how I intend to test the broader claim that these mechanisms improve outcomes.</p></div></div></aside>
