_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35572:@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35573: status: published
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35574: heroImage: "/assets/posts/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain/hero-governed-cube.png"
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35575: heroAlt: "A shared capability pattern connects several project workbenches, each retaining a distinct adaptation."
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35576:+heroPlacement: frontispiece
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35577: whyItMatters: "Approval attaches to an artifact. Its use happens in a context that approval never saw. A current registry can coexist with stale deployed instructions and unacceptable outcomes."
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35578: leaderTakeaway: "Require four separate assurances: pinned artifact identity, authorized conditions of use, evidence of actual execution, and an accepted outcome. Connect the systems responsible for each."
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35579: relatedSlugs:
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35580:@@ -378,6 +379,8 @@
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35581: 
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35582: These are dated implementation records, summarized as methods. The August commits establish when checks entered the repository; the September audit establishes what that later inspection found. Neither date silently becomes the incident date or an attestation of today's runtime state.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35583: 
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35584:+[Read the full receipt set in Evidence Focus.](/essays/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain/evidence/)
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35585:+
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35586: <Evidence kind="observed" /> **The reviewer copy.** The drift-check source records a deployed reviewer missing its mandatory establish-the-diff step while the upstream copy contained it. The incident was filed August 5; the check was committed August 6. Its five-day interval describes the stale deployment. Comparing deployed bytes with the source makes that discrepancy visible, but doesn't recover a per-session loading history or count incorrect reviews.[^drift]
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35587: 
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/taste-fix-codex.log:35588: <Evidence kind="observed" /> **Sibling instructions.** One harness-specific instruction file carried superseded doctrine for six weeks after its canonical sibling changed. The parity gate committed August 5 checks a declared relationship between those files. It doesn't require every document to be identical. The separate live-document staleness check catches a named obsolete assertion outside that pair; it leaves dated historical records alone.[^parity][^staleness]
